w-parser-output .cs1-maint{color:#18911f}}@media screen and (prefers-color-scheme:dark){html.skin-theme-clientpref-os .mw-parser-output .cs1-maint{color:#18911f}}</style><cite class=\"citation web cs1\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://developer.apple.com/library/mac/documentation/Cocoa/Conceptual/ObjCRuntimeGuide/Articles/ocrtVersionsPlatforms.html\">\"Runtime Versions and Platforms\"</a>. <i>Developer.apple.com</i>. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20160720034718/https://developer.apple.com/library/mac/documentation/Cocoa/Conceptual/ObjCRuntimeGuide/Articles/ocrtVersionsPlatforms.html\">Archived</a> from the original on July 20, 2016<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">December 24,</span> 2017</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.jtitle=Developer.apple.com&amp;rft.atitle=Runtime+Versions+and+Platforms&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fdeveloper.apple.com%2Flibrary%2Fmac%2Fdocumentation%2FCocoa%2FConceptual%2FObjCRuntimeGuide%2FArticles%2FocrtVersionsPlatforms.html&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AObjective-C\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-lattner2014-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-lattner2014_2-0\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFLattner2014\" class=\"citation web cs1\">Lattner, Chris (June 3, 2014). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://nondot.org/sabre/\">\"Chris Lattner's Homepage\"</a>. Chris Lattner. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20140604061001/http://nondot.org/sabre/\">Archived</a> from the original on June 4, 2014<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">June 3,</span> 2014</span>. <q>The Swift language is the product of tireless effort from a team of language experts, documentation gurus, compiler optimization ninjas, and an incredibly important internal dogfooding group who provided feedback to help refine and battle-test ideas. Of course, it also greatly benefited from the experiences hard-won by many other languages in the field, drawing ideas from Objective-C, Rust, <a href=\"/wiki/Haskell\" title=\"Haskell\">Haskell</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Ruby_(programming_language)\" title=\"Ruby (programming language)\">Ruby</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Python_(programming_language)\" title=\"Python (programming language)\">Python</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/C_Sharp_(programming_language)\" title=\"C Sharp (programming language)\">C#</a>, CLU, and far too many others to list.</q></cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=Chris+Lattner%27s+Homepage&amp;rft.pub=Chris+Lattner&amp;rft.date=2014-06-03&amp;rft.aulast=Lattner&amp;rft.aufirst=Chris&amp;rft&#95;id=http%3A%2F%2Fnondot.org%2Fsabre%2F&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AObjective-C\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-3\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFApple&#95;Developer2013\" class=\"citation web cs1\">Apple Developer (April 23, 2013). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/Cocoa/Conceptual/ObjectiveC/Introduction/introObjectiveC.html\">\"The Objective-C Programming Language (Introduction)\"</a>. <a href=\"/wiki/Apple_Inc.\" title=\"Apple Inc.\">Apple Inc.</a> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20181026174828/https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/Cocoa/Conceptual/ObjectiveC/Introduction/introObjectiveC.html\">Archived</a> from the original on October 26, 2018<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">February 15,</span> 2025</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=The+Objective-C+Programming+Language+%28Introduction%29&amp;rft.pub=Apple+Inc.&amp;rft.date=2013-04-23&amp;rft.au=Apple+Developer&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fdeveloper.apple.com%2Flibrary%2Farchive%2Fdocumentation%2FCocoa%2FConceptual%2FObjectiveC%2FIntroduction%2FintroObjectiveC.html&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AObjective-C\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-4\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-4\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite id=\"CITEREFSingh2003\" class=\"citation web cs1\">Singh, Amit (December 2003). <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://osxbook.com/book/bonus/ancient/whatismacosx/history.html\">\"A Brief History of Mac OS X\"</a>. Mac OS X Internals. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20120514135706/http://osxbook.com/book/bonus/ancient/whatismacosx/history.html\">Archived</a> from the original on May 14, 2012<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">June 11,</span> 2012</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=A+Brief+History+of+Mac+OS+X&amp;rft.pub=Mac+OS+X+Internals&amp;rft.date=2003-12&amp;rft.aulast=Singh&amp;rft.aufirst=Amit&amp;rft&#95;id=http%3A%2F%2Fosxbook.com%2Fbook%2Fbonus%2Fancient%2Fwhatismacosx%2Fhistory.html&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AObjective-C\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite&#95;note-:0-5\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><b><a href=\"#cite_ref-:0_5-0\">^</a></b></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" /><cite class=\"citation web cs1\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation#app-frameworks\">\"App Frameworks\"</a>. Apple. June 2014. <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20190216075924/https://developer.apple.com/documentation/#app-frameworks\">Archived</a> from the original on February 16, 2019<span class=\"reference-accessdate\">. Retrieved <span class=\"nowrap\">February 13,</span> 2019</span>.</cite><span title=\"ctx&#95;ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft&#95;val&#95;fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=unknown&amp;rft.btitle=App+Frameworks&amp;rft.pub=Apple&amp;rft.date=2014-06&amp;rft&#95;id=https%3A%2F%2Fdeveloper.apple.com%2Fdocumentation%23app-frameworks&amp;rfr&#95;id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AObjective-C\" class=\"Z3988\"></span></span>\n</li>\n</ol></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nParsed by mw‐api‐ext.eqiad.main‐77d9d4c448‐xhz6z\nCached time: 20260918164233\nCache expiry: 1063051\nCache expiry source: Template:Years_or_months_ago (currentmonth)\nReduced expiry: true\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1]\nCPU time usage: 0.198 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.252 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1155/1000000\nRevision size: 5396/2097152 bytes\nPost‐expand include size: 25268/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 2983/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 18/100\nExpensive parser function count: 7/500\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 17937/5000000 bytes\nLua time usage: 0.134/10.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 4418390/52428800 bytes\nNumber of Wikibase entities loaded: 0/500\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%  235.165      1 -total\n 35.85%   84.312